amengo/Palmeiras in this FIFA dataset (it's FIFA 19-era, mostly European clubs). So \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\" would return empty — fine, we answer from data. Wait — maybe there are more clubs. Let me check for other Brazilian clubs: \"São Paulo\"? It didn't appear. Let me check \"Flamengo\" — not present. OK so the FIFA dataset (FIFA 19) has limited Brazilian clubs. Fine.\n\n- FIFA has 827 Brazilian players nationally.\n\nTeam name normalization challenges:\n- Brasileirao_Matches: \"Palmeiras-SP\" style, unaccented? \"Atletico-MG\" (no accent). Check for accented names in that file: maybe \"Avai-SC\" or \"Avái\"? Let me check.\n- BR-Football: \"Sao Paulo\", \"Atletico Mineiro\", \"Gremio\", \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\", \"Botafogo RJ\", \"EC Bahia\", \"Athletico Paranaense\"? Different naming: \"Atletico Mineiro\" vs \"Atletico-MG\" vs \"Athletico-PR\" vs novo \"Athletico-PR\"?\n- novo: \"Guarani\", \"Athletico-PR\", \"Grêmio\" (accented!), \"América-MG\"?\n\nI need a canonical name mapping. Approach: normalize function that:\n1. Lowercases\n2. Removes accents (via unicodedata NFKD)\n3. Removes common suffixes/prefixes: state suffix after hyphen (-SP), \"RJ\" suffix at end (\"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" → \"vasco da gama\"), \"(antigo ...)\" parentheticals, \"EC\"/\"SC\"/\"AC\" prefixes? Hmm \"EC Bahia\" → \"bahia\"? That could conflict... but \"Bahia\" in other files is \"Bahia-BA\". Fine → \"bahia\".\n4. Common alias mapping for tricky ones:\n   - \"atletico mineiro\" / \"atletico-mg\" → \"atletico-mg\" (canonical \"Atlético Mineiro\"? display \"Atlético-MG\")\n   - \"athletico-pr\" / \"athletico paranaense\" / \"atletico paranaense\"? Note: Athletico-PR was renamed from Atlético-PR in 2019. In BR-Football dataset what's used? Let me check: probably \"Athletico Paranaense\". I'll map both to same canonical.\n   - \"america-mg\" / \"america mineiro\"\n   - \"botafogo rj\" / \"botafogo\"\n   - \"vasco da gama\" / \"vasco\"\n   - \"coritiba\", \"cruzeiro\", etc. straightforward.\n   - \"sport\" / \"sport recife\" — in BR-Football maybe \"Sport Recife\".\n   - \"ponte preta\", \"portuguesa\".\n   - \"ceara\" / \"Ceará\".\n   - \"sao paulo\" straightforward after de-accenting.\n   - \"gremio\" / \"Grêmio\" — de-accent handles.\n   - \"avai\" / \"Avaí\".\n   - \"fortaleza\" — maybe \"Fortaleza EC\" in some file?\n   - \"goias\" / \"Goiás\".\n   - \"chapecoense\", \"criciuma\", etc.\n\nCanonical display names: I'll keep a display map with proper accents for well-known clubs, and a key map (de-accented lowercase).\n\nLet me enumerate distinct team names per file to build a robust normalizer. Let me dump distinct names from each file.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b68715e001x1M8j5cp2mZuki","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","messageID":"msg_05b682e6300127mX44T2a62yk7"}}
