iants (set of raw names), match_count, competitions (set), seasons (min, max).\n- Also clubs_index: core → list of entries (for stateless lookups).\n- Resolve(query): parse query → core/state; if state present → exact key match; if no state → all entries with that core; if multiple, sort by match_count desc, return top + others as alternatives. If no core match → substring/fuzzy match (difflib.get_close_matches) across cores and variants.\n\nDisplay names: for major clubs, curated display map with proper accents: Flamengo, Fluminense, Palmeiras, Corinthians, São Paulo, Santos, Grêmio, Internacional, Cruzeiro, Atlético-MG, Athletico-PR, Botafogo, Vasco da Gama, Bahia, Vitória, Sport, Ceará, Fortaleza, etc. Fallback: the most \"decorated\" raw variant (max accented chars, then most common). I'll write: choose raw variant with highest count of non-ascii chars; tie-break by frequency.\n\nMatch model fields: date (datetime.date or None), datetime?, home, away, home_goals, away_goals, competition (canonical), season, round/stage, venue?, source file, extra stats (corners/shots/attacks for BR-Football), ht results.\n\nCompetition canonicalization:\n- input aliases: \"brasileirao\", \"brasileirão serie a\", \"serie a\", \"campeonato brasileiro\", \"serie-a\" → \"serie_a\"; \"serie b\" → \"serie_b\"; \"serie c\"; \"copa do brasil\", \"brazilian cup\", \"cdb\" → \"copa_do_brasil\"; \"libertadores\", \"copa libertadores\", \"conmebol\" → \"libertadores\".\n- Display: \"Brasileirão Série A\", \"Copa do Brasil\", \"Copa Libertadores\", \"Série B\", \"Série C\".\n\nCompetition source mapping (for standings + queries):\n- serie_a: Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2023) + novo (2003-2019). Overlap 2012-2019! Dedup needed for combined queries? For search_matches with competition=serie_a, showing both sources' same matches would duplicate (Palmeiras 2023 appears in both Brasileirao_Matches and BR-Football \"Serie A\"). Hmm. BR-Football Serie A — which seasons? Let me check season range. If 