lap Brasileirao_Matches seasons? Check: BR-Football date range. Let me verify seasons: bras 2012-2023, BR-Football Serie A maybe 2012-2023 as well. Also novo 2003-2019 overlaps bras 2012-2019! So dedup matters there too: for serie_a seasons 2012-2019, bras wins (priority), novo's dropped. And cup: Brazilian_Cup_Matches vs BR-Football \"Copa do Brasil\" overlap → cup file wins.\n\nFor per-competition season availability: serie_a: 2003-2023 (novo 2003-2011 + bras 2012-2023), serie_b/c: BR-Football only, copa_do_brasil: cup file 2012-2023 (+ brf fallback), libertadores: 2013-2023?\n\nAlso note: search by competition \"all\" — search across everything (deduped union). The union dedup should handle a match appearing in both bras and novo (same match). Dedup key must normalize team names to canonical keys. Dates: novo DD/MM/YYYY parsed to date; bras has datetime; date part equal. Good.\n\nRisk: same fixture played twice in a season legitimately (e.g., Copa do Brasil home/away two legs — same teams both directions, fine; but same home/away same season twice could happen in knockout two-leg... no, two legs are reversed home/away. Repeated identical home/away/season occurs in... Brasileirão no. Copa do Brasil: team A home vs B twice in same season? No, legs alternate. But same-date-ish? Use (season, date, home_key, away_key) — distinct legs differ by date. Edge: BR-Football rows have exact dates; novo has Data; bras datetime→date. OK.\n\nHmm wait — actually there's a subtlety: Copa do Brasil in cup file rounds 1-8; two legs alternate. Dedup fine.\n\nBut what about Libertadores same-season two legs — alternate home/away. Fine.\n\nWhat about matches where date is missing? Check for missing dates/goals in files. Libertadores goals are quoted strings (\"2\") — parse ints. Some rows may have empty goals? Need robust parsing: skip rows without valid goals for stats? Let me check data cleanliness quickly.\n\nAlso BR-Football goals are floats (\"1.0\") → int.\n\nFIFA parsing: keep s