             delta=abs((a[1]-b[1]).days)\n                deltas[delta]+=1\n                if delta==0 and (a[2],a[3])!=(b[2],b[3]): same_date_diff_score+=1\nprint(\"groups:\",len(grp),\"multi-entry groups:\",multi)\nprint(\"delta distribution (top):\", deltas.most_common(15))\nprint(\"same-date different-score:\", same_date_diff_score)\n# how many groups have same score but delta>2?\nfar=0\nfor k,v in grp.items():\n    for i in range(len(v)):\n        for j in range(i+1,len(v)):\n            a,b=v[i],v[j]\n            if a[1] and b[1] and (a[2],a[3])==(b[2],b[3]) and abs((a[1]-b[1]).days)>2: far+=1\nprint(\"same-score pairs with delta>2:\", far)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788240433496,"end":1788240433502}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting! Dates mostly align (score mismatches: just 1 — the 2016 Chapecoense vs Atletico-MG match which in bras has empty goals? Wait: bras entry ('bras', ..., None, None) — bras has a row with empty goals for that match (the Chapecoense plane crash aftermath? Actually the 2016 Chapecoense round was affected by the crash — their last match wasn't played; bras has the row with empty goals, novo says 0-0? Hmm actually wait, novo has 0-0 and bras has empty. Interesting: this reveals bras has some rows with empty goals — the unplayed final round(s) of 2016 (Chapecoense crash). Need to handle None goals (skip from stats).\n\nBut look at the mismatch pattern: 2012: 38 novo rows NOT deduped against bras (i.e., 418 total for a 380-match season → 38 duplicates from novo with DIFFERENT dates or different teams keys?). 2013: 91 dupes, 2014: 91+279... The date alignment between novo and bras is imperfect — novo dates differ for some matches (e.g., postponed matches recorded differently, or my parse wrong?). Hmm 38 in 2012... Also brf doesn't align well either (279 of 380 aligned in 2014).\n\nSo date-based dedup leaves significant duplicates. Total serie_a 12248 vs expected: 2003-2021 by novo/bras = 9*~380+... expected unique ≈ 552+552+462+380*8(2006-2013?) hmm let me compute expected: 2003:552(46 teams?), 2004:552? (24 teams×46=552?), 2005:462, 2006-2023: 380×18=6840. Total = 552+552+462+6840 = 8406. We got 12248 — way over. Duplicates ~3800. That's a lot of dupes. Date mismatch: novo vs bras — maybe novo uses the ORIGINAL scheduled date while bras uses... hmm, or my date parse of novo is day/month swapped? \"29/03/2003\" → 29 March ✓.\n\nWait, maybe the issue is different: 2012 bras has 380 matches; novo 2012 should also have 380; only 342 aligned (38 dupes). That means 38 matches have different dates between the two files. Postponed? 10% is plausible-ish for a season? Hmm no — maybe some matches in novo are at different dates due to stadium changes etc. But 38/380=10%.\n\nAnd brf 2014: only 101 of 380 aligned (279 dupes!). brf dates might systematically differ (brf date might be the scheduled date; 279/380 differing is a LOT). Something systematic. Maybe brf date is often different by a day or two.\n\nAlternative dedup key: (competition, season, home_key, away_key) — without date! For a league season, each pair meets exactly twice (home/away) — but the same pairing home+away appears twice as DIFFERENT keys (A|home, B|away) vs (B|home, A|away) — distinct. So (comp, season, home_key, away_key) is nearly unique per league fixture. Exception: Copa do Brasil? No — cup pairings alternate home/away within a round; two legs = 2 matches with swapped keys. Same key twice in a cup season could happen only if two separate rounds pair the same teams (e.g., teams meet in round 2 AND final — possible! e.g. Flamengo vs Cruzeiro twice in different rounds with same home team? Both legs home for same team? Rounds have 2 legs (A home, then B home) → keys differ. But meeting in two different rounds: round X: A home vs B; round Y (later): A home vs B again! That CAN happen in Copa do Brasil (e.g., 2019? teams can meet twice in different phases? Actually yes possible). Risk of over-dedup: dropping a legitimate second meeting with same home team. Hmm.\n\nFor serie_a league: safe — each (season, home, away) exactly once.\nFor copa_do_brasil: possible collision across rounds.\nFor libertadores: group stage + knockouts — same pairing can occur in group (2 legs, alternating) and again in knockout (alternating) — same home team could host twice in a season (e.g., group: A hosts B; knockout semi: A hosts B again). POSSIBLE.\n\nSo dedup key needs round-awareness for cups: (comp, season, round, home_key, away_key)? But rounds differ between cup file (numeric 1-8) and brf Copa do Brasil (no round column!). brf has no round for Copa do Brasil. Ugh.\n\nBetter dedup strategy: date-based BUT with fuzzy date window: if same (comp, season, home, away) with dates within ±2 days → duplicate. Let me check: what's the date delta distribution for same (comp,season,home,away) pairs? Let me measure: group by (comp,season,home,away), collect dates+sources, see deltas.\n\nAlso for cross-source score consistency: 1 mismatch only (2016 crash match). Good sign.\n\nActually maybe better: dedup key (comp, season, home_key, away_key, round_bucket) where round_bucket = round number when both known, else ordinal index of the pairing? Complex.\n\nSimplest robust: per (comp, season, home_key, away_key) group — normally size ≤2 (league: 1 per orientation; cups: 1 per orientation per meeting). For cups a same-orientation repeat across rounds is rare. Within a group, dedup matches that are \"the same fixture\": same score AND dates within 3 days → same; if same score but far dates → probably genuinely two different meetings (keep both); if different dates & scores → keep both.\n\nLet me measure the date deltas for groups that have >1 entry with same (comp, season, orientation) to see if ±3 days catches the brf/bras novo dupes.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b6f4c16001qVKNjiQIReyRC0","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","messageID":"msg_05b6ed1dd0019gpX