. Group all matches by (comp, season, home_key, away_key).\n2. Within group, canonical key: prefer sources in priority order [bras=0, cup=0, lib=0, novo=1, brf=2]. Sort group by priority.\n3. Merge: iterate sorted list; a new entry is a duplicate of an existing kept entry if scores equal (or one has None) and |date delta| ≤ 2 days. If None vs played: treat as dup, keep played version.\n   Careful ordering when merging None: bras(None) then novo(0-0): keep... we want the played score. Rule: when merging, keep the entry with non-None goals if the other has None; otherwise keep the earlier-priority one.\n4. For matches with no date (e.g. lib 'NA' season row has no date? it has datetime? the NA-season final row: datetime empty? Let me check: the row has '-' goals and season NA — datetime? It printed stage final; its datetime might be empty). If date missing, dedup by (comp, season, hk, ak, score) exact-only.\n\nNow expected results: serie_a totals after merge should be ~552,552,462,380×18=8406 total; copa: cup file 1337 + brf 1123 (2014-2023; overlap 2014-2021 ~ aligned/unaligned mix) → merged total should be ~1337 + (2022: 2023 brf copa matches ~ 78+?) ≈ 1337+154? brf copa 2014-2021 subset ≈ 1123-154=969, most of which dedupe against cup file (some with delta>2 kept → slight overcount). Let me verify after implementing.\n\nAlso note: 2016 Chapecoense — bras has rows with empty goals. How many empty-goal rows in bras? Check. These \"unplayed\" rows: novo recorded 0-0 (interesting). For stats, exclude None-goal matches. Let me count empty goals in bras & cup & lib.\n\nAlso there may be more empty-goal rows (e.g. 2016 Chapecoense cancelled round). Check quickly. Also the lib NA row: check its datetime.\n\nThen build the package. Let me now write all the code. Files as planned. I'll be careful and thorough. Let me check the remaining unknowns (bras empty goals, lib NA row datetime, cup empty goals) then write code.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b6fd7930014t