own, team (resolved display), opponent, competition, season, truncated:bool}.\n  Sort: date desc (None dates last), then competition. Limit default 20 (max 200).\n- last_match_between: search h2h matches, pick max date with goals not None (played); return match + note about next/latest scheduled if unplayed newer. \"When did Flamengo last play Corinthians? What was the score?\" ✓.\n- head_to_head: all matches between a & b (any comp/season filters); wins/draws/losses counted only PLAYED matches; goals for each; list recent first (limit param default 20).\n- team_stats: filters; venue in {'home','away','all'}: for 'home' → matches where team_key == home_key etc. Compute played, w/d/l, gf, ga, win rate. Also breakdown per venue always? Return both overall and home/away splits for 'all'. Include per-competition split when no competition given? Provide `by_competition` list. Good for \"Performance by competition\".\n- team_profile: club info: display, key, state, country, variants (name variations seen), competitions with counts + season ranges, overall record (all comps), goals, seasons active. ✓ \"What competitions has Palmeiras played in?\"\n- standings: comp must be serie_a/b/c (league) — copa/libertadores → error with explanation (knockout). season required. Compute from played matches. Sort standard. Champion top; relegated = bottom 4 (note: modern standard). Also produced `rows` with all fields. Validate: 2019 serie_a flamengo 90 pts.\n  For serie_a seasons covered by multiple sources — deduped list ✓ 380 games. For 2022: bras NA rows (81) — brf provides played → merged → 380 played ✓ good. 2023: brf 377 → standings still computable (note incompleteness? 377/380 — fine, no note needed; but let me add a note when matches < expected? skip).\n- biggest_wins: margin = |hg-ag| desc, then goals desc; filter played; comp/season optional; return top N with margin.\n- competition_stats: given comp (+season) or all comps: matches played count, avg goals/match, home win %, draw %, away win %, avg home goals, avg away goals, biggest win ref. For 'all' → overall + per-comp breakdown. ✓ \"average goals per match in the Brasileirão\", \"Home win rate: 47.3%\".\n- derbies: DERBIES list of (name, keyA, keyB). Filter season optional; return per derby: matches found (recent first, limit 5 each) + h2h counts. ✓ \"Show me all derbies in 2023\".\n- player_search: params name/nationality/club/position/min_overall/max_overall/order/limit. Position accepts code or group. Returns players list (dicts), total, criteria echo. Sorting default overall desc, tie name.\n- player_club_report: params nationality optional, min_overall optional → groups.\n- list_competitions: comps with display, seasons (sorted list), match counts, description, sources.\n- list_teams: comp/season optional → clubs with match counts (all clubs or filtered by participation). For season+comp → participants with counts.\n- resolve helper exposure: `resolve_team` public for CLI/tests.\n\nMatch dict shape (for output):\n```json\n{\"competition\":\"serie_a\",\"competition_display\":\"Brasileirão Série A\",\"season\":2019,\"date\":\"2019-09-03\",\"time\":\"20:00\",\"home\":\"Flamengo\",\"away\":\"Fluminense\",\"home_goals\":2,\"away_goals\":1,\"score\":\"2-1\",\"round\":\"22\",\"stage\":null,\"phase\":\"Round 22\",\"venue\":null,\"source\":\"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\",\"stats\":{...} or null}\n```\nphase display: for lib: stage; for series: f\"Round {round}\"; cup: f\"Round {round}\" or \"Final\" when final round. Compute \"is_final\" for cup? render uses phase string. For cup final rounds → phase \"Final (round 8)\". Hmm — the round→final mapping per season computed at load: cup_final_round[season] = max round. Then phase for those matches = \"Final\". I'll compute during loading and store match.round_display. OK.\n\n### render.py\n\nFunctions returning human-readable strings for each query result (used by MCP text + CLI stdout):\n- render_match_line(m): \"2019-09-03: Flamengo 2-1 Flum