**: novo \"Bahia\" has Mandante_UF = \"BH\"?? The novo file's UF column uses \"BH\" for Bahia (typo in dataset!) — BA vs BH. Let me check what UF values novo uses. Similarly \"Vitória\" → novo says UF \"ES\"?? novo-only shows 'vitoria|ES' 179 — meaning novo assigns ES to Vitória (wrong — Vitória is BA!). Hmm wait, or is it right? Vitória (BA) vs Rio Branco-ES... novo \"Vitória\" 179 matches with UF ES?! That's a data error in novo (or their \"Vitória\" really means... no, Vitória-BA played Serie A 2004-2019... 179 ≈ 4.7 seasons — plausible BA). Let me check novo UF values distribution per team. Bahia→BH typo; Vitória→ES? weird.\n\n2. **bras \"Atletico-PR\" vs novo \"Athletico-PR\"**: my alias only maps ('athletico',None)→('atletico','PR') — but novo \"Athletico-PR\" WITH state PR → core 'athletico' state PR — no alias for ('athletico','PR')! I need ALIAS ('athletico','PR') → ('atletico','PR'). Wait no — my ALIAS maps ('athletico paranaense','PR') → ('atletico','PR') but bare ('athletico','PR') isn't aliased. In the earlier full-data test I DID have ('athletico', None)→... hmm in the last scratch I dropped some aliases. In the SECOND scratch (the delta analysis) I had `('athletico',None):('atletico','PR')`? No — I had ('athletico paranaense','PR'), ('athletico paranaense','PR'), ('athletico mineiro','MG') and ('athletico mineiro',None)... The delta analysis scratch (third script) had ALIAS with ('athletico mineiro','MG') etc but NOT bare 'athletico'. Hmm — and in that run the merge groups worked? It showed multi-entry groups 2792 with deltas — the 'athletico|PR' vs 'athletico|PR'... bras \"Atletico-PR\" → ('atletico','PR') key atletico|PR; novo \"Athletico-PR\" → deaccent → 'athletico-pr' → tokens ['athletico','pr'] → state PR, core 'athletico' → key atletico|PR. SAME! Wait — deaccent('Athletico-PR') = 'athletico-pr' — the ' Athletico' loses its h? NO — deaccent removes combining marks; 'Athletico' has no accents at all! It's just spelled \"Athletico\" (with h) vs \"Atletico\" (without h). These are DIFFERENT WORDS: Athletico vs Atletico! My aliases never map bare 'athletico'+'PR'... So novo Athletico-PR → core 'athletico'|PR and bras Atletico-PR → core 'atletico'|PR — DIFFERENT keys. Need alias ('athletico','PR')→('atletico','PR') or better: unify 'athletico' → 'atletico' globally (name spelled both ways for the same club — the club was renamed Atlético→Athletico in 2019 but it's the same entity; for a knowledge graph we want ONE node).\n\n3. **'red bull bragantino|SP' vs 'bragantino|SP'**: bras-only shows 'red bull bragantino|SP' — my alias ('red bull bragantino','SP')→('bragantino','SP') existed in scratch 2 but NOT in the last scratch. My bad. Keep alias.\n\n4. **'cuiaba|MT' vs ...?** bras-only 'cuiaba|MT' 76 — novo doesn't have Cuiabá (joined Serie A 2021 — novo ends 2019; 76 = 2 seasons × 38 ✓ no overlap issue). Not a problem — it's bras-only because novo has none. Same for 'guarani|SP', 'paysandu|PA', 'sao caetano|SP', 'brasiliense|DF', 'america|RN', 'ipatinga|MG', 'barueri|SP', 'santo andre|SP', 'gremio prudente|SP' — novo-only because those clubs don't appear in bras era (2003-2011 clubs). Those are FINE (no overlap conflict). The problematic ones are where BOTH sources have the club but keys differ: 'bahia|BA' vs 'bahia|BH' (novo UF typo 'BH'), 'vitoria|ES' (novo UF for Vitória = ES?!). Let me verify novo's UF for Bahia and Vitória rows.\n\nSo real fixes needed:\n- ALIAS ('athletico','PR') → ('atletico','PR'). Or normalize 'athletico'→'atletico' as core-alias regardless of state. I'll add core spelling aliases: {'athletico':'atletico'} applied always.\n- ('red bull bragantino','SP') → ('bragantino','SP') + stateless variant.\n- novo UF corrections: map state 'BH'→'BA' (dataset typo). And check Vitória: novo UF says ES?? Let me check the actual rows. If novo really tags Vitória as ES, then novo \"Vitória\"+ES vs bras \"Vitoria-BA\"... → keys vitoria|ES vs vitoria|BA mismatch → duplicates for Vitória matches 2004-2019 (which overlap bras 2012-2019 → ~8 seasons of dupes!). Earlier 2012 analysis: only bahia mismatched (38) — 2012 Vitória wasn't in Serie A. For 2013-2019, Vitória IS in Serie A (2013,2017,2018...) → dupes. Need fix: state correction table for novo? Or generic: when a state code isn't a valid UF ('BH'), map BH→BA. For Vitória-ES: hmm — maybe novo really means Vitória-ES?? No — Vitória-ES is a tiny club never in Serie A. It's a dataset error. How to fix robustly? A \"state correction\" by (core, wrong_state) → right_state: ('bahia','BH'→'BA'), ('vitoria','ES'→'BA')?? But careful: legit vitoria|ES exists in cup/brf data (\"Vitoria F. C. - ES\", \"Vitoria ES\")! If I remap ALL vitoria|ES→BA, the legit ES club gets merged into BA. BAD.\n\n  Better: remap only for the novo source. The novo loader can apply per-source state fixes: in novo, Bahia's UF 'BH'→'BA'; Vitória's UF 'ES'→'BA'?? Hmm is novo's Vitória UF really ES? Let me check raw rows. Alternatively ignore novo's UF for team-state and use my own resolution: for novo rows, parse_club(team_name, state_hint=UF) but with fallback: if the resulting key conflicts... complex.\n\n  Simplest correct approach: per-source UF fix map for novo: {'BH':'BA'} and check what novo uses for Vitória. Let me look at the actual data: novo rows for Vitória home → Mandante_UF value.\n\nAlso check other novo UF oddities: list all (team, UF) pairs from novo where UF not in STATES or where same team has multiple UFs.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b759d8f001Sc82WKh2IrHKMx","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","messageID":"msg_05b752e9c001Lola2ISbhhQoon"}}
