ally has 380/380 orientations — so union should be 380. The scratch's 381 was caused by the phantom athletico-paranaense key (cup 2016 'Atlético Paranaense - PR' → alias missing in scratch → phantom + extra orientations... wait cup isn't serie_a. Hmm — 2016 381: novo 380 orientations, bras 380 orientations — union after resolution should be ≤380. 381 means one phantom: e.g. 'america|MG'? no... Actually 2016: novo 'Athletico-PR' → CORE_ALIAS athletico→atletico → atletico|PR ✓; bras 'Atletico-PR' → atletico|PR ✓. Hmm — maybe the Chapecoense unplayed row: bras 'Chapecoense-SC' vs 'Atletico-MG' NA (kept, no goals) + novo 0-0 (kept because league rule picks first-with-goals — novo 0-0 has goals → best=novo... wait the league rule picks best = first WITH goals by priority: bras NA (no goals), novo 0-0 (goals) → novo picked → 1 row. Fine.\n\nWhatever — the real implementation will be verified with real tests. 2016 should come out at 380 or 381; I'll check and assert accordingly (data truth). Actually, let me think: could 381 be from the phantom 'athletico paranaense|'? cup 2016 'Atlético Paranaense - PR' — in scratch the ALIAS[('athletico paranaense','PR')] WAS set at the end... so cup resolved ✓. serie_a 2016 sources: bras + novo only (brf starts 2014 — brf 2016 Serie A EXISTS! brf covers 2014-2023!). So brf 2016 'Athletico Paranaense' stateless → phantom key → all 38 brf Athletico matches keyed to phantom → orientations involving phantom ≈ 38-ish, minus merging with... bras/novo orientations don't involve the phantom → union = 380 + 38 - (phantom-vs-phantom?) ≈ 418?? But scratch showed 381. Confusing — because SOME brf matches merged (those whose opponents resolved)... no wait — orientation (phantom, X) never equals (atletico|PR, X). Hmm, so union should be ~380+38=418 for 2016 with a full phantom... but scratch showed 381 for 2016 and 407 for 2019 (not 418). So in the scratch the phantom must be a club present in only SOME seasons' brf data... \n\nENOUGH. The scratch alias table was inconsistent across runs; I can't reverse-engineer it. The real code will have a complete alias table and I'll assert exact counts in tests based on what the real code produces — with sanity bounds (e.g., 2014-2022 within [377, 382], 2003: 552 etc.). For the headline test (2019 = 380 & Flamengo 90 pts) I'm confident the real implementation will produce it (each source individually has 380 orientations for 2019? bras 2019: 380; novo 2019: 380; brf 2019: 379... union with full resolution = 380).\n\nTime to write the package for real. Layout:\n\nbrazilian_soccer_mcp/\n- __init__.py\n- normalizer.py\n- models.py\n- loader.py\n- queries.py\n- render.py\n- tools.py\n- server.py\n- cli.py\n- __main__.py\ntests/\n- conftest.py\n- test_normalizer.py\n- test_loader.py\n- test_queries_matches.py\n- test_queries_teams.py\n- test_queries_players.py\n- test_queries_competitions.py\n- test_queries_stats.py\n- test_sample_questions.py\n- test_server.py\npyproject.toml\nREADME.md (update)\n\nWrite each file carefully now. Start with normalizer.py — the foundation.\n\nKey detail decisions for normalizer:\n- `parse_club_name(raw, state_hint=None)` → ClubIdentity(core, state, country) with full alias table.\n- State detection: after deaccent/casefold/parenthetical-removal, token-based.\n- NEWO UF fixes handled in loader (source-specific), not normalizer.\n- `canonical_club_key(identity)` → f\"{core}|{state or country or ''}\".\n- Competition aliases.\n- Date parsing: parse_date supporting 3 formats + optional time extraction.\n- Money parsing for FIFA values.\n\nFORM_WORDS_FRONT = {'ec','sc','fc','ce','ge','ca','ad','se','aa','ac','cd'? no,'sport','club','clube','futebol','ltda','grêmio'? no}\nWait — front 'sport' is dangerous (\"Sport Boys\"); I protect 'sport boys'. Any other 'sport X'? \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" (protect handled by alias after strip), \"Sport Recife\" (alias BEFORE strip). So front-strip 'sport' is OK given those two protections (alias-before-strip for 'sport recife', protect 'sport boys'). What about \"Sporting Cristal\" — token 'sporting' ≠ 'sport' ✓ safe. \"Sport Boys\" protected ✓.\n\nFORM_WORDS_BACK = {'ec','sc','fc','ce','ge','ca','ad','se','aa','club','clube','futebol','ltda','esporte','esportivo'}? 'esportivo' back: \"Esportivo Bento Goncalves\"? brf 'Esportivo Bento Goncalves' — FRONT 'esportivo'! Add 'esportivo' to front too. \"Esportivo - RS\" (cup): single token 'esportivo' — no strip (len 1) ✓ distinct club.\n\nAlso strip back 'c'? single-letter trailing handled. 'sa'? \"Palmas Ltda\" → 'ltda' back → 'palmas' ✓.\n\nTrailing 's.c'/'f.c'/'s.c.': dots stripped → 'sc'/'fc' form words ✓.\n\nPROTECTED = {'sport boys'} (skip form stripping entirely).\n\nALIASES (exact, applied pre- and post-form-strip on (name,st)):\nFull table (careful, complete):\n```\n('atletico mineiro','MG') -> ('atletico','MG')\n('atletico mineiro',None) -> ('atletico','MG')\n('athletico paranaense','PR') -> ('atletico','PR')   # 2019+ spelling\n('atletico paranaense','PR') -> ('atletico','PR')\n('athletico paranaense',None) -> ('atletico','PR')\n('atletico paranaense',None) -> ('atletico','PR')\n('athletico',None) -> ('atletico','PR')   # bare, Libertadores\n('atletico goianiense','GO') -> ('atletico','GO')\n('atletico goianiense',None) -> ('atletico','GO')\n('atletico acreano','AC') -> ('atletico','AC')       # brf full name\n('atletico alagoinhas','BA') -> ('atletico','BA')\n('atletico cearense','CE') -> ('atletico','CE')\n('atletico soro?? no\n('corinthians paulista',None) -> ('corinthians','SP')\n('corinthians paulasta','SP') no — spelled paulista\n('corinthians paulista','SP') -> ('corinthians','SP')\n('vasco da gama','RJ') -> ('vasco','RJ')\n('vasco da gama',None) -> ('vasco','RJ')\n('vasco',None) -> ('vasco','RJ')\n('sport recife',None) -> ('sport','PE')\n('sport recife','PE') -> ('sport','PE')\n('sport',None) -> ('sport','PE')\n('nautico capibaribe',None) -> ('nautico','PE')\n('portuguesa desportos',None) -> ('portuguesa','SP')\n('portuguesa santista'?? not present, skip\n('red bull bragantino','SP') -> ('bragantino','SP')\n('red bull bragantino',None) -> ('bragantino','SP')\n('bragantino',None) -> ('bragantino','SP')\n('america de natal','RN') -> ('america','RN')\n('america de natal',None) -> ('america','RN')\n('america fc natal','RN') -> ('america','RN')\n('america fc natal',None) -> ('america','RN')\n('america rico'? no\n('clube do remo',None) -> ('remo','PA')\n('clube do remo','PA') -> ('remo','PA')\n('guarani de juazeiro','CE') -> ('guarani','CE')\n('guarani de juazeiro',None) -> ('guarani','CE')\n('ser caxias','RS') -> ('caxias','RS')\n('ser caxias',None) -> ('caxias','RS')\n('operario ferroviario','PR') -> ('operario','PR')\n('operario ferroviario',None) -> ('operario','PR')\n('operario ferloviario esporte c','PR') -> ('operario','PR')  # typo'd raw in cup — but form strip handles 'esporte c'... token 'ferloviario' typo differs from 'ferroviario'! cup writes \"Operario Ferloviario Esporte C - PR\"? Actually the cup list showed 'Operario Ferroviario Esporte C - PR' — spelled right. brf has 'Operario Ferroviario Esporte C' too. OK skip typo variant.\n('sao francisco do xingu'? no\n('sfrancisco','PA') -> ('sao francisco','PA')   # from \"S.francisco - PA\"\n('sousa','PB') -> ('souza','PB')\n('xv piracicaba','SP') -> ('xv de piracicaba','SP')\n('xv piracicaba',None) -> ('xv de piracicaba','SP')\n('xv de piracicaba',None) -> ('xv de piracicaba','SP')?? stateless: cup has 'Xv de Piracicaba - SP' suffixed; brf 'XV Piracicaba' stateless → alias (None) ✓\n('gremio novorizontino',None) -> ('novorizontino','SP')\n('gremio novorizontino','SP') -> ('novorizontino','SP')\n('novorizontino',None) -> ('novorizontino','SP')\n('desportiva ferroviaria','ES') -> ('desportiva','ES')\n('desportiva ferroviaria',None) -> ('desportiva','ES')\n('real noroeste capixaba','ES') -> ('real noroeste','ES')\n('real noroeste capixaba',None) -> ('real noroeste','ES')\n('santa quiteria futebol clube','MA')? form strip handles → 'santa quiteria' ✓ no alias needed\n('inter de limeira',None) keep distinct ✓\n('independiente del valle' vs 'independiente del valle' same after casefold ✓\n('tolima',None) vs ('deportes tolima',None) → unify: ('deportes tolima',None)->('tolima',None)\n('universitario per')? country suffix handles ✓\n('nacional uru') ✓ country\n('guarani par') ✓\n('libertad par') ✓\n('olimpia par') ✓\n('delfin equ') ✓\n('river plate uru') ✓ country distinguishes from ARG river plate ✓\n('boavista sport club',...) → form strip ✓\n('juventude ma')? distinct ✓ (state MA)\n('sao jose poa','RS')? 'POA' not state — special: map state 'POA'→'RS' before detection? The raw is \"Sao Jose - POA\" → trailing token 'poa' not in STATES → stays in core: 'sao jose poa'. Add alias ('sao jose poa',None)->('sao jose','RS'). ✓\n('macae esporte',None)->('macae','RJ')? brf 'Macae Esporte FC'/'Macae Esporte RJ' — the RJ one suffixed ✓; 'Macae Esporte FC' stateless → strip 'fc' → 'macae esporte' → alias → ('macae','RJ'). Add.\n('ceo varzeagrandense',None) keep.\n('tuntum',None) keep ('tuntum EC' → 'tuntum').\n('serra f c es'?? \"Serra F. C. - ES\" → tokens serra f c → dots → 'f','c' single letters... wait 'f.'→'f', 'c.'→'c' — single-letter strip only TRAILING while >1: ['serra','f','c'] → drop 'c' → ['serra','f'] → drop 'f' → ['serra'] ✓.\n('aquidauanense futebol clube','MS') → form strip ✓\n('sao domingos futebol clube','SE') ✓\n('paulista futebol clube','SP') → 'paulista' ✓\n('arapongas esporte clube','PR') → 'arapongas' ✓\n('santa cruz futebol clube'?? not present\n('operario ferloviario esporte c','PR')?? skip\n('independiente de tucurui'?? 'Independente de Tucuruí - PA' vs brf 'Independente PA' — different cores ('independente de tucurui' vs 'independente'). Alias ('independente de tucurui','PA')->('independente','PA')? Both small; add for correctness.\n('independente',None)->('independente','PA')\n('boavista',None)->('boavista','RJ')\n('desportiva',None)->('desportiva','ES')\n('abc',None)->('abc','RN')? \"Abc - RN\" suffixed; brf 'ABC' stateless → alias ✓\n('asa',None)->('asa','AL')  # brf 'ASA','ASA AL' ✓\n('crb',None)->('crb','AL')\n('csa',None)->('csa','AL')\n('cs alagoano'?? brf 'CS Alagoano' = CSA! → tokens cs alagoano → alias ('cs alagoano',None)->('csa','AL') add.\n('c.r.b.'→dots→'crb' ✓\n('remo',None)->('remo','PA')\n('sampaio correa',None)->('sampaio correa','MA')\n('ceara',None)->('ceara','CE')  # brf stateless 'Ceara'\n('vitoria',None)->('vitoria','BA')  # FIFA + brf stateless → BA (famous) — hmm dominance would also give BA ✓ but FIFA club resolution goes through resolve() anyway... For queries the FIFA club resolution uses the registry resolver (dominance). The alias is a safety net; fine.\n('bahia',None)->('bahia','BA')\n('vila nova',None)->('vila nova','GO')\n('gama',None)->('gama','DF')\n('brasiliense',None)->('brasiliense','DF')\n('ipatinga',None)->('ipatinga','MG')\n('barueri',None)->('barueri','SP')\n('gremio prudente',None)->('gremio prudente','SP')\n('santo andre',None)->('santo andre','SP')\n('sao caetano',None)->('sao caetano','SP')\n('guarani',None)->('guarani','SP')  # novo stateless? novo has UF hints; cup 'Guarani - SP' suffixed; dominance gives SP anyway ✓\n('juventude',None)->('juventude','RS')  # dominance also RS ✓ (vs Juventude-MA suffixed)\n('chapecoense',None)->('chapecoense','SC')  # dominance ✓\n('criciuma',None)->('criciuma','SC')\n('figueirense',None)->('figueirense','SC')\n('coritiba',None)->('coritiba','PR')\n('parana',None)->('parana','PR')  # FIFA 'Paraná' ✓\n('avai',None)->('avai','SC')\n('goias',None)->('goias','GO')\n('cuiaba',None)->('cuiaba','MT')\n('fortaleza',None)->('fortaleza','CE')\n('oeste',None)->('oeste','SP')?? 'Oeste SP' suffixed in brf; cup 'Oeste - SP' ✓; dominance SP ✓ — add? fine add.\n('noroeste',None)->('noroeste','SP')? cup 'Noroeste - SP' ✓ suffixed. skip.\n('marilia',None)->('marilia','SP')? skip — dominance handles.\n```\n\nHmm — I'm duplicating what dominance resolution does. STRATEGY: aliases only for names where dominance CANNOT infer the state (because no suffixed variant of that core exists anywhere, e.g. 'atletico mineiro' → core after alias 'atletico' has suffixed variants ✓ so dominance CAN map ('atletico mineiro' stateless → core 'atletico mineiro' — dominance maps core 'atletico mineiro' → nothing! The pre-alias core is 'atletico mineiro', and no suffixed variant of core 'atletico mineiro' exists (suffixed variants are 'Atletico-MG' → core 'atletico'). So 'atletico mineiro' stateless needs EXPLICIT alias. Same class: 'atletico goianiense', 'sport recife', 'athletico paranaense', 'america de natal', 'america fc natal', 'clube do remo', 'portuguesa desportos', 'nautico capibaribe', 'gremio novorizontino', 'red bull bragantino', 'corinthians paulista', 'ser caxias', 'operario ferroviario', 'desportiva ferroviaria', 'real noroeste capixaba', 'sfrancisco', 'xv piracicaba', 'macae esporte', 'cs alagoano', 'independente de tucurui', 'deportes tolima', 'sao jose poa', 'vasco da gama' (core 'vasco da gama' stateless — dominance for core 'vasco da gama'? NO suffixed 'vasco da gama - RJ' → parse → state RJ core 'vasco da gama'!! WAIT — \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" tokens ['vasco','da','gama','rj'] → state RJ core 'vasco da gama' — the SUFFIXED variant HAS core 'vasco da gama'! So dominance DOES map core 'vasco da gama' → RJ ✓. And brf 'Vasco Da Gama RJ' → state RJ detected → core 'vasco da gama' + RJ ✓ then needs UNIFYING with 'vasco|RJ' from novo/lib — so alias ('vasco da gama','RJ')→('vasco','RJ') still needed to merge cores 'vasco da gama' vs 'vasco'. Similarly ('atletico mineiro','MG')→('atletico','MG') merges with ('atletico','MG') from 'Atletico-MG'. These MERGE-aliases are needed regardless of state.)\n\nSo the alias table serves two purposes: (1) merge different cores of the same club; (2) stateless full names → canonical. Keep the full table.\n\nThen dominance (core→state from all data) handles remaining stateless cores (brf bare 'Santos' etc.).\n\nNow — dominance resolution correctness concern: resolve() must be used EVERYWHERE keys are computed (matches AND registry AND queries). Centralize: normalizer exposes `ClubNormalizer` class that wraps the two-pass logic:\n- Pass A (register): feed (raw, state_hint) → identity; accumulate core→state counts (only when state known post-alias).\n- Pass B (finalize): for each identity, if state None & core has dominant state → adopt it.\n- The loader runs pass A while reading rows, calls finalize, then computes canonical keys for all rows (store identities alongside; recompute key after finalize).\n- `resolve_query(name)` for user queries: parse → if state known → key; else dominant or fuzzy.\n\nRegistry keyed by canonical key.\n\nAlso handle 'poa'→RS and 'vn' (\"Rio Branco - Vn - ES\" → tokens rio branco vn → trailing 'vn'?? 'vn' not state; core 'rio branco vn' → alias → ('rio branco','ES')). Add.\n\nOK — writing the real code now. Also remember: display names. DISPLAY_OVERRIDES dict for major clubs keyed by (core, state).\n\nFor time budget: I've spent a lot on analysis; now write efficiently. Files one by one.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b7c5c5c001AwXzeeepFhb78T","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","messageID":"msg_05b7b544c001T3sgWC0KVs4x00"}}
