ulo|SP' vs 'sao paulo|' stateless keys coexisting?\n\nThe bug hypothesis: In `_raw_rows`, for brf rows I set home_state/away_state = None. In `load_dataset`, pass 1: `normalizer.register(raw, state_hint)` — brf 'Sao Paulo' → identity ('sao paulo', None) — no vote. Bras 'Sao Paulo-SP' → ('sao paulo','SP') vote ✓. finalize → dominant['sao paulo']='SP'. Pass 2: `row[side_key] = row[side_identity].key()` — BUT `row[side_identity]` was computed during PASS 1 via `normalizer.register()` which calls `parse_club_name` WITHOUT dominance resolution! I stored the identity from register() and never re-resolved via `normalizer.identity()` in pass 2! The key() of the pass-1 identity is stateless for brf names. THAT'S THE BUG. Pass 2 must call `normalizer.identity(raw, state_hint)` fresh (or normalizer.key(raw, hint)).\n\nFix: in load_dataset pass 2:\n```python\nfor row in rows:\n    for side in (\"home\",\"away\"):\n        ident = normalizer.identity(row[f\"{side}_raw\"], row[f\"{side}_state\"])\n        row[f\"{side}_key\"] = ident.key()\n        row[f\"{side}_identity\"] = ident\n        if ident.region and not row[f\"{side}_state\"]:\n            row[f\"{side}_state\"] = ident.region\n```\n\nThat should fix it. Then 2014-2022 should be ~380 and 2009 = 379 (data truth), 2016 = 380 or 381.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b881ee8001kaI1Y8Rxf3AekN","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","messageID":"msg_05b87ef21001veqUAv5ka6j7uu"}}
