_key, m.away_key, m.home_goals, m.away_goals) for m in via_h2h}\nkeys_search = {(m['competition'], m['season'], m['date'], m['home_key'], m['away_key'], m['home_goals'], m['away_goals']) for m in via_search['matches']}\nprint(\"only in h2h:\", keys_h2h - keys_search)\nprint(\"only in search:\", keys_search - keys_h2h)\nfor m in via_h2h:\n    k=(m.competition, m.season, str(m.date), m.home_key, m.away_key, m.home_goals, m.away_goals)\n    if k not in keys_search:\n        print(\"MISSING FROM SEARCH:\", m.competition, m.season, m.date, m.home, m.score, m.away, m.source)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788242333364,"end":1788242333387}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Excellent — nearly everything works and matches history (2019 table EXACTLY matches the spec's example: Flamengo 90, Santos 74 (22W,8D,8L), Palmeiras 74 (21W,11D,6L) — the spec example says exactly this!). Copa finals 2012-2020 exactly 2 per season ✓; 2021 has none (incomplete data) ✓. Libertadores finals correct including the None-season unplayed row ✓.\n\nIssues found:\n1. **`resolve_team(ds, 'Sport Club Corinthians Paulista')` → None!** The alias ('corinthians paulista', None) → parse: \"sport club corinthians paulista\" → tokens [sport, club, corinthians, paulista] → state None → pre = 'sport club corinthians paulista' → ALIAS lookup (pre, None) — NOT in table (I only have ('corinthians paulista', None)). Form-strip front: 'sport' stripped, 'club' stripped → 'corinthians paulasta'... wait tokens become [corinthians, paulasta]? no — [corinthians, paulista] → core 'corinthians paulista' → ALIAS ('corinthians paulista', None) → ('corinthians','SP') ✓ — but it returned None! Why? OH — the front-strip of 'sport'... the _PROTECTED_CORES check: `if pre not in _PROTECTED_CORES` — pre = 'sport club corinthians paulasta'?? no 'sport club corinthians paulista' not protected → strip proceeds. Hmm — but wait, the ALIAS-before-strip lookup uses (pre, state) = ('sport club cor