-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py\n@@ -83,10 +83,11 @@\n     {\"AC\",\"AL\",\"AP\",\"AM\",\"BA\",\"CE\",\"DF\",\"ES\",\"GO\",\"MA\",\"MT\",\"MS\",\"MG\",\"PA\",\n      \"PB\",\"PR\",\"PE\",\"PI\",\"RJ\",\"RN\",\"RS\",\"RO\",\"RR\",\"SC\",\"SP\",\"SE\",\"TO\"}\n )\n \n-#: Foreign country suffixes used by the Libertadores dataset.\n-COUNTRY_ABBREVS = frozenset({\"uru\", \"par\", \"equ\", \"per\", \"ven\"})\n+#: Foreign country suffixes used by the Libertadores dataset (uppercase,\n+#: matched against the upper-cased token).\n+COUNTRY_ABBREVS = frozenset({\"URU\", \"PAR\", \"EQU\", \"PER\", \"VEN\"})\n \n #: Club-organisation words stripped from the front/end of a name while at\n #: least one meaningful token remains (\"EC Bahia\" -> \"bahia\",\n #: \"Fortaleza FC\" -> \"fortaleza\").  'sport' is front-strippable (see the\n","additions":3,"deletions":2},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalizer.py","time":{"start":1788242400641,"end":1788242400643}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Found it! `parse_club_name(\"Nacional (URU)\")` → country=None, core='nacional' — the parenthetical handling DIDN'T set country! Why? Look at the code:\n\n```python\nfor content in _PAREN_RE.findall(text):\n    token = content.replace(\".\", \"\").strip()\n    if len(token) == 2 and token.upper() in STATE_ABBREVS:\n        state = state or token.upper()\n    elif len(token) == 3 and token.upper() in COUNTRY_ABBREVS:\n        country = token.upper()\n```\ncontent='URU' → len 3, upper 'URU' in COUNTRY_ABBREVS ✓ → country='URU'. But result shows country=None!! So this loop never matched... unless — `text = squash(raw)` — squash REPLACES apostrophes and casefolds... \"(URU)\" stays \"(uru)\" → findall gives 'uru' ✓. Hmm — len('uru')==3 ✓ 'URU' in {'uru','par','equ','per','ven'}? COUNTRY_ABBREVS = frozenset({\"uru\",\"par\",\"equ\",\"per\",\"ven\"}) — LOWERCASE strings! And I check `token.upper() in COUNTRY_ABBREVS` — 'URU'.upper() = 'URU' ∉ {'uru',...}!! Mismatch: set is lowercase but comparison uses .upper(). STATE_ABBREVS are uppercase and compared with .upper() ✓ fine. COUNTRY_ABBREVS lowercase + upper compare → NEVER matches. Same bug in the trailing-token branch: `tokens[-1].upper() in COUNTRY_ABBREVS` → never matches → 'nacional-uru' → core 'nacional uru' (as seen).\n\nFix: make COUNTRY_ABBREVS uppercase strings: {\"URU\",\"PAR\",\"EQU\",\"PER\",\"VEN\"} — and keep comparisons .upper(). Also dominance-region assignment in identity(): `if region in STATE_ABBREVS: state=... else: country=...` — region 'URU' ∉ STATES → country='URU' ✓ works once regions are uppercase.\n\nAlso registry has 'nacional uru|' phantom — after fix it becomes 'nacional|URU' ✓. This also affects other lib clubs: \"Barcelona-EQU\" → currently core 'barcelona equ' phantom; \"Guaraní-PAR\" → 'guarani par'... and \"River Plate-URU\" → 'river plate uru'. All become proper country keys after fix. Also '(PAR)' parentheticals.\n\nFix now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b8d8ff5001sy7wGZ3W1QEDrF","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","messageID":"msg_05b8d6d240019W7m21WAeSsEnp"}}
