{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788242652519,"sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-afa8141a90e348f5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import load_dataset\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.queries import standings, list_competitions\nds = load_dataset()\nr = standings(ds, 'serie_b', 2019)\nprint(\"serie_b 2019 top3:\", [(x['position'], x['team'], x['points'], x['played']) for x in r['rows'][:3]])\nlc = list_competitions(ds)\nprint([(c['id'], c['first_season'], c['last_season'], c['matches']) for c in lc['competitions']])\nEOF"},"output":"serie_b 2019 top3: [(1, 'Red Bull Bragantino', 75, 38), (2, 'Sport Recife', 68, 38), (3, 'Coritiba', 66, 38)]\n[('serie_a', 2003, 2023, 8402), ('serie_b', 2014, 2023, 3655), ('serie_c', 2014, 2023, 1749), ('copa_do_brasil', 2012, 2023, 1656), ('libertadores', 2013, 2022, 1255)]\n","metadata":{"output":"serie_b 2019 top3: [(1, 'Red Bull Bragantino', 75, 38), (2, 'Sport Recife', 68, 38), (3, 'Coritiba', 66, 38)]\n[('serie_a', 2003, 2023, 8402), ('serie_b', 2014, 2023, 3655), ('serie_c', 2014, 2023, 1749), ('copa_do_brasil', 2012, 2023, 1656), ('libertadores', 2013, 2022, 1255)]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import load_dataset\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.queries import standings, list_competitions\nds = load_dataset()\nr = standings(ds, 'serie_b', 2019)\nprint(\"serie_b 2019 top3:\", [(x['position'], x['team'], x['points'], x['played']) for x in r['rows'][:3]])\nlc = list_competitions(ds)\nprint([(c['id'], c['first_season'], c['last_season'], c['matches']) for c in lc['competitions']])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788242652494,"end":1788242652518}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Two assertions to verify:\n1. `by_id[\"serie_a\"][\"matches\"] == 8402` — earlier output said serie_a matches: 8402? The list_competitions run earlier printed ('serie_a', 2003, 2023, 8402) — hmm wait, that run was BEFORE the country fix; after the country fix total matches stayed 16717. serie_a count: 552+552+462+380*13(2006-2018? let me count: 2006-2022 = 17 seasons, minus 2009 anomaly)... 552+552+462 = 1566; 2006-2022: 17 seasons × 380 = 6460 minus 1 (2009=379) = 6459; +2023: 377 → total = 1566+6459+377 = 8402 ✓.\n2. `test_serie_b_standings` — champion assertion `result[\"champion\"][\"team\"] == \"Flamengo\" or position == 1` — sloppy tautology. Série B 2019 champion real-world: Flamengo?? no — Série B 2019 champion was... Bragantino? Yes! RB Bragantino won Série B 2019. But data (brf) — let me check what brf says. If brf's Série B 2019 is fine, champion should be Bragantino (SP). Let me verify quickly and assert exactly.\n3. lib first_season — after country fix, seasons: 2013-2022 + None (excluded from seasons_for). first 2013 ✓.\n\nCheck Série B 2019 champion + also verify Copa finals test values remain stable (2012-2020 = 2 each — after country fix? country fix only affects lib foreign keys; copa unchanged ✓). Also test_queries_matches asserted `per_season.get(2021, 0) == 0` — cup 2021 final rounds: earlier output showed 2012-2020 with 2 each ✓ and 2021: 1 unplayed leg (the merged final first leg?). Wait — cup_final_rounds for 2021: max round with ≤2 matches... earlier (pre-fix) run said \"cup final 2021 round 4 (Fluminense vs Criciúma)\" — that was the pre-mislabel-fix state. NOW with the current code: 2021 max round — the cup file 2021 rounds: 1-6 with the semis at 7? Let me recheck the copa finals per season now (the last verification run showed: cup finals per season: {2012: 2, ..., 2020: 2} — NO 2021 entry ✓, and search total 18 = 9 seasons × 2 ✓).\n\nLet me verify Série B 2019 champion.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b916416001fuNHZzf0wDP8Og","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","messageID":"msg_05b913d2c001uWLJc2ZQOU8j8t"}}
