n definition order? Actually pytest runs classes in file order (definition). TestInitialize creates its OWN servers ✓. TestToolListing: `test_tools_list_shape` initializes id=0 ✓ then test_ping ✓. OK.\n\nBut wait — one potential issue: `TestToolCalls.test_search_matches_call` — if TestToolListing somehow didn't run first (e.g. -k filter), the module fixture server isn't initialized → -32002. Fine under full runs. To be safe, make the module fixture self-initializing: in the fixture, call handle(initialize) once. Let me update the fixture: after creating MCPServer, do `srv.handle(_request(0, \"initialize\", {}))`. But _request is defined at module level before fixture ✓.\n\nAlso check: server fixture is module-scoped and creates MCPServer(dataset=load_dataset()) — loads dataset at fixture creation (~0.8s) ✓.\n\nNow: pyproject.toml, README update, then run the tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b948cc9001UzWuaq0c6hrDvl","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","messageID":"msg_05b946d59001ajHZGioETWxcj1"}}
