{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788243187363,"sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bbfb22118a4f216d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/tests/test_server.py","newString":"        def send_raw(self, text: str) -> None:\n            self.process.stdin.write(text)\n            self.process.stdin.flush()\n\n        def talk(self, message: dict) -> dict | None:\n            \"\"\"Send a request and read its one response line.\"\"\"\n            self.send_raw(json.dumps(message) + \"\\n\")\n            return self.read()\n\n        def notify(self, message: dict) -> None:\n            \"\"\"Send a notification (no response is ever written).\"\"\"\n            self.send_raw(json.dumps(message) + \"\\n\")\n\n        def read(self) -> dict | None:\n            line = self.process.stdout.readline()\n            return json.loads(line) if line.strip() else None","oldString":"        def send_raw(self, text: str) -> None:\n            self.process.stdin.write(text)\n            self.process.stdin.flush()\n\n        def talk(self, message: dict) -> dict | None:\n            self.send_raw(json.dumps(message) + \"\\n\")\n            return self.read()\n\n        def read(self) -> dict | None:\n            line = self.process.stdout.readline()\n            return json.loads(line) if line.strip() else None"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/tests/test_server.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/tests/test_server.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/tests/test_server.py\n@@ -360,11 +360,16 @@\n     self.process.stdin.write(text)\n     self.process.stdin.flush()\n \n def talk(self, message: dict) -> dict | None:\n+    \"\"\"Send a request and read its one response line.\"\"\"\n     self.send_raw(json.dumps(message) + \"\\n\")\n     return self.read()\n \n+def notify(self, message: dict) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Send a notification (no response is ever written).\"\"\"\n+    self.send_raw(json.dumps(message) + \"\\n\")\n+\n def read(self) -> dict | None:\n     line = self.process.stdout.readline()\n     return json.loads(line) if line.strip() else None\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/tests/test_server.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/tests/test_server.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/tests/test_server.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-7a36b7336902/tests/test_server.py\n@@ -360,11 +360,16 @@\n     self.process.stdin.write(text)\n     self.process.stdin.flush()\n \n def talk(self, message: dict) -> dict | None:\n+    \"\"\"Send a request and read its one response line.\"\"\"\n     self.send_raw(json.dumps(message) + \"\\n\")\n     return self.read()\n \n+def notify(self, message: dict) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Send a notification (no response is ever written).\"\"\"\n+    self.send_raw(json.dumps(message) + \"\\n\")\n+\n def read(self) -> dict | None:\n     line = self.process.stdout.readline()\n     return json.loads(line) if line.strip() else None\n \n","additions":5,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"tests/test_server.py","time":{"start":1788243187360,"end":1788243187361}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"pytest hung — probably the end-to-end subprocess test: `session.read()` blocks on readline() when the server writes no response (e.g. for a notification, no response is written → readline blocks forever waiting for the notification's response). In `test_full_session`, after initialize I call `session.talk(notifications/initialized)` → talk() WRITES the notification AND THEN READS a line — but notifications produce no output → readline blocks → hang!\n\nFix: talk() should only read when a response is expected. Add `notify(message)` (write only) and use it for the notification. Or make talk take `expect_response=True`. Let me restructure: `talk(msg, expect=True)`.\n\nAlso check the server process itself isn't hanging on something else — the parse-error test: send_raw(\"this is not json\\n\") → server responds -32700 ✓ response expected. Empty line: no response; my test sends \"\\n\" then immediately `talk(ping)` which writes ping and reads — the pending output is the ping response ✓ fine (only one read).\n\nAlso first kill the hung pytest process (the bash tool terminated it, but the spawned subprocess may linger). Let me check for stray processes and fix the test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b9989e6001D4gqsYMoA7oTqE","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","messageID":"msg_05b996c8e001fo44FGQYEfzp4H"}}
