ed rows... OR Serie B 2019 actually had 20 teams but brf has 2 extra (phantom) — positions show 'Paraná' at 6th and 'América Mineiro' 5th — América-MG played Série B 2019 ✓ (relegated 2018), Paraná ✓ Série B 2019. Hmm 22 teams — was Série B 2019 20 teams? Yes, Série B is always 20. So brf 2019 Serie B includes 2 extra teams. Which? Let me check. Could be Série C teams mislabeled ('Série B' rows for C clubs) — but my mislabel filter only covers competitions with primary sources (serie_a). Serie B has no primary. 22 teams — let me list them and find the 2 extras (probably two Série C clubs mislabeled, or botafogo SP...). Actually — WAIT: Série B 2019: let me list real participants: Bragantino, Sport, Coritiba, América-MG, Paraná, Cuiabá?, ..., Boa Esporte?... Real 2019 Série B (20): Bragantino, Sport, Coritiba, Paraná, América-MG, Cuiabá, CRB, Figueirense, Ceará? no Ceará was A... hmm. Let me just get the 22 from data and figure out which 2 are extra. Then decide: extend the mislabel filter for serie_b/serie_c cross-consistency? Principle: for serie_b seasons, if a club appears in brf's serie_c for the same season MORE... no — a club can't be in both B and C same season. The 2 extras probably also appear in Serie C 2019 → cross-competition conflict within brf: same season, club in BOTH serie_b and serie_c lists → the smaller set is mislabeled? Or drop from B if their serie_c count is much larger (38 vs few). Rule: for each season and club, if brf lists the club in TWO different divisions, keep the division where the club has a full-ish season (≥30 matches) and drop the other. That's principled: a club can't play two divisions in one season; the ~38-match one is the truth.\n\nLet me look at the data first.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b9a485c001SMdQjoGpmYibaZ","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","messageID":"msg_05b9a0ca5001gSboN9CBlHyD2C"}}
