e:\n+            key = (row[\"competition\"], row[\"season\"])\n+            appearances[key][row[\"home_key\"]] += 1\n+            appearances[key][row[\"away_key\"]] += 1\n+\n+    kept: list[dict] = []\n+    for row in phase_one:\n+        if (row[\"competition\"] in _LEAGUE_COMPETITIONS\n+                and row[\"season\"] is not None):\n+            counts = appearances[(row[\"competition\"], row[\"season\"])]\n+            if (counts[row[\"home_key\"]] < _MIN_LEAGUE_APPEARANCES\n+                    or counts[row[\"away_key\"]] < _MIN_LEAGUE_APPEARANCES):\n+                continue  # state-league fixture mislabeled as a league game\n         kept.append(row)\n     return kept\n \n \n","additions":35,"deletions":7},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/loader.py","time":{"start":1788243266778,"end":1788243266780}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The 2 extras: `suzano|SP: 1` and `guarulhos|SP: 1` — single matches each! Those are Paulistão (state championship) matches mislabeled as \"Serie B\" in brf (Suzano-SP and Guarulhos-SP are tiny São Paulo clubs that played the state league, NOT Série B). Also notice `brasil de pelotas|` — stateless key! \"Brasil de Pelotas\" — brf name; core 'brasil de pelotas' with no state → no suffixed variant anywhere → stays stateless key 'brasil de pelotas|' ✓ fine (unique club, consistent).\n\nFix approach for the 1-match phantoms: extend the mislabel guard — for league competitions WITHOUT a primary source (serie_b, serie_c, and serie_a seasons not covered by primary), a brf row is suspicious if the club has only a handful of matches in that competition-season while the competition norm is ~38. Principled rule: within a (competition, season) of a league, clubs whose appearance count is below some small threshold (say < 8, i.e. clearly not a season-long participant) are dropped — their fixtures are mislabeled state-league/cup rows. But careful: 2003 Série A had 46 teams all with 552-count high; every legit league participant plays ≥ 2×(teams-1)... minimum realistic: Série A 2023 partial (377) still gives everyone ≥ 37. For any league season, legit participants have ≥ ~30 matches (even in shortened seasons). A club with 1-2 matches in a league season = mislabel. But dropping based on count requires two passes (count then filter) — implement as part of _drop_mislabeled_league_rows second phase: for league rows from ANY source (well, brf mainly), compute per (comp, season, club) appearance counts within that competition-season; drop rows where either club's count < 8. Threshold 8 is safe (no legit league participant has < 8; even in weird cases like 2016 Chapecoense 38 ✓; novo 2003 46 teams → 46 games each ✓; teams relegated mid... no such thing).\n\nWait — but careful about applying to serie_a primary seasons too: e.g. copa-mislabeled... the count rule applies to league comps only ✓. And the 2019 serie_a brf rows for legit clubs: all ~38 ✓ unaffected.\n\nAlso apply to novo/bras? They're primary and accurate; the count rule would only drop if a club appears < 8 times in a league season from those sources — no such case. Apply uniformly (source-agnostic, league comps only).\n\nImplementation: in `_drop_mislabeled_league_rows` — rename to `_clean_league_rows`: \nPhase 1: primary-participation filter (existing).\nPhase 2: appearance-count filter: counts = Counter over league rows per (comp, season) for home/away keys; a row survives only if home count ≥ 8 AND away count ≥ 8. Hmm — but a phantom row inflates a legit club's count too (Botafogo-SP got 38 real + maybe 1 phantom vs Suzano) — threshold 8 is way below so fine.\n\nEdge: 2019 serie_b: suzano 1, guarulhos 1 → all their rows dropped (2 matches) → 20 teams ✓. Also these 2 rows added +1 to some legit teams (38+1?) — brf shows several 38 — hmm 38 matches in a 20-team league = correct full season; the phantom matches involved... suzuki vs who? If Suzano played Botafogo-SP, Botafogo-SP count = 39? It shows 38. So phantom rows paired suzano vs guarulhos with each other only? 2 matches (home/away between the two phantoms) → legit clubs unaffected ✓✓.\n\nNow the 'a'/'b'/'c' alias greed bug in normalize_competition: restrict substring fallback to aliases with length ≥ 4. Fix.\n\nAlso fix the 3 test issues:\n- test_curated_aliases: use ClubNormalizer for stateless full names.\n- test_registry Palmeiras seasons: 2004 not 2003 (Série B 2003 not in dataset — Palmeiras WAS in Série B 2003, cool detail to document).\n- test_serie_b_standings: after fix, 20 teams and Bragantino 75 ✓.\n- test_search_matches_call: fix \"Total\" assertion (truncated case).\n- test_standings spec-format: adjust substring.\n- test_last_match_pair_without_history: use Flamengo vs Sampaio Corrêa.\n- test_unknown_and_all & test_invalid_competition: fixed by the alias-greed fix.\n\nAlso the pytest warning: class-scoped fixture as instance method — move `session` fixture to module level (outside class). Let me restructure: define Session class + session fixture at module scope.\n\nImplement all fixes now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b9a9fb800165w4qjCe5tzS3f","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","messageID":"msg_05b9a545f001ew64muosnTRTWd"}}
