{"type":"text","timestamp":1788243645978,"sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","part":{"id":"prt_05ba0858a001RBfn3lBmbk37ra","messageID":"msg_05ba07289001GzIHt5JZit0es2","sessionID":"ses_fa4988af5ffe6mID1MhYqXoot3","type":"text","text":"Done. Everything in TASK.md is implemented and verified:\n\n**Deliverables**\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/` — zero-dependency Python package: `normalizer.py` (team-name/competition/date normalization), `loader.py` (all 6 CSVs, cross-source dedup, club registry, indexes), `models.py`, `queries.py` (14 query functions), `render.py` (spec-format answers), `tools.py` (MCP tool catalogue), `server.py` (MCP stdio server — newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 on the stdlib), `cli.py`\n- `tests/` — 148 BDD/GWT-structured pytest scenarios (Gherkin docstrings, one feature module per TASK.md capability) — **all passing in ~4s**; `ruff check` + `ruff format` clean\n- `pyproject.toml` + updated `README.md`\n\n**Run it**\n```bash\npython -m brazilian_soccer_mcp                                   # MCP server (stdio)\npython -m brazilian_soccer_mcp.cli standings serie_a 2019        # direct CLI\npython -m pytest\n```\n\n**Notable engineering** (validated against ground truth): the three overlapping match sources dedup to exactly 380 matches per Série A season 2006-2022; source data errors repaired (novo's Bahia=\"BH\"/Vitória=\"ES\" UFs, BR-Football's mislabeled Série B fixtures and stray state-league rows); 'NA'/'-' goals treated as unplayed and excluded from stats; stateless names resolve by dominance (\"Santos\"→Santos-SP). Computed standings reproduce real history — 2019: Flamengo 90 pts (28W 6D 4L), exactly the spec's example — and performance criteria hold (initialize 37 ms, queries in single-digit ms, load 0.8 s).","time":{"start":1788243641738,"end":1788243645976}}}
